-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Answers are `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or a MAYBE of a type): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING elsewhere.

§ `Section 742.4 -- Supervisor may propose changes to optional conditions`

DECLARE `s 742.4(1) recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.4(1) the offender`
    `s 742.4(1) the prosecutor`
    `s 742.4(1) the court`
    `s 742.4(1) someone else`

-- src:15948 | 742.4 (1) Where an offender’s supervisor is of the opinion that a change in circumstances makes a change to the optional conditions desirable, the supervisor shall give written notification of the proposed change, and the reasons for it, to the offender, to the prosecutor and to the court.
@ref s 742.4(1) (src:15948)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 742.4(1) recipient`
      `the supervisor is of the opinion that a change in circumstances makes a change to the optional conditions desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.4(1) the supervisor shall give written notification of the proposed change, and the reasons for it, to the recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the supervisor is of the opinion that a change in circumstances makes a change to the optional conditions desirable`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offender's supervisor is of the opinion that a change in circumstances makes a change to the optional conditions desirable" (a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF recipient EQUALS `s 742.4(1) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the duty names the offender, the prosecutor and the court; it does not say that no one else is notified
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `742.4(2) The request or order for a hearing`

DECLARE `s 742.4(2)(a) requester` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.4(2)(a) the offender`
    `s 742.4(2)(a) the prosecutor`
    `s 742.4(2)(a) someone else`

-- src:15950 | (2) Within seven days after receiving a notification referred to in subsection (1),
-- src:15951 | (a) the offender or the prosecutor may request the court to hold a hearing to consider the proposed change, or
@ref s 742.4(2)(a) (src:15950-15951)
GIVEN requester IS A `s 742.4(2)(a) requester`
      `the days after receiving the notification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.4(2)(a) the requester may request the court to hold a hearing to consider the proposed change` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the days after receiving the notification` GREATER THAN 7
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within seven days after receiving a notification" (a period in the text's own words; a "within" gate on a "may", listed, group (i))
        IF requester EQUALS `s 742.4(2)(a) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the offender or the prosecutor may request"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15950 | (2) Within seven days after receiving a notification referred to in subsection (1),
@ref s 742.4(2) (src:15950)
-- src:15952 | (b) the court may, of its own initiative, order that a hearing be held to consider the proposed change,
@ref s 742.4(2)(b) (src:15952)
GIVEN `the days after receiving the notification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.4(2)(b) the court may, of its own initiative, order that a hearing be held to consider the proposed change` MEANS
    IF `the days after receiving the notification` AT MOST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within seven days after receiving a notification" (a period in the text's own words; a "within" gate on a "may", listed, group (i))

-- src:15953 | and a hearing so requested or ordered shall be held within thirty days after the receipt by the court of the notification referred to in subsection (1).
@ref s 742.4(2) (src:15953)
GIVEN `the days from the receipt by the court of the notification to the hearing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.4(2) a hearing so requested or ordered is held in time` MEANS
    IF `the days from the receipt by the court of the notification to the hearing` AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be held within thirty days after the receipt by the court of the notification" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a))

DECLARE `s 742.4(2) act` IS ONE OF `s 742.4(2) hold the hearing`

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The clock is in days from the receipt by the court of the notification.
-- src:15953 | and a hearing so requested or ordered shall be held within thirty days after the receipt by the court of the notification referred to in subsection (1).
@ref s 742.4(2) (src:15953)
`s 742.4(2) the court shall hold the hearing so requested or ordered` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 742.4(2) hold the hearing`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the hearing was not held within thirty days after the receipt by the court of the notification"

