§ `Section 742.5 -- Transfer of order`

-- src:15967 | (1.1) The transfer may be granted only with
-- src:15968 | (a) the consent of the Attorney General of the province in which the conditional sentence order was made, if the two territorial divisions are not in the same province; or
-- src:15969 | (b) the consent of the Attorney General of Canada, if the proceedings that led to the issuance of the conditional sentence order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 742.5(1.1) (src:15967-15969)
GIVEN `the two territorial divisions are in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings that led to the order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.5(1.1) the transfer may be granted with the consents given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((NOT (`the two territorial divisions are in the same province`)) AND `the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made consented`)
           OR (`the proceedings that led to the order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` AND `the Attorney General of Canada consented`)
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text reads "(a) ... ; or (b) ...": one consent that the case calls for is enough (fork F-5: the other reading requires every consent the case calls for)
        IF (NOT (`the two territorial divisions are in the same province`)) OR `the proceedings that led to the order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The transfer may be granted only with (a) the consent of the Attorney General of the province ... or (b) the consent of the Attorney General of Canada"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither paragraph's case is present, and the subsection names no consent for it

-- src:15965 | 742.5 (1) Where an offender who is bound by a conditional sentence order becomes a resident of a territorial division, other than the territorial division where the order was made, on the application of a supervisor, the court that made the order may, subject to subsection (1.1), transfer the order to a court in that other territorial division that would, having regard to the mode of trial of the offender, have had jurisdiction to make the order in that other territorial division if the offender had been tried and convicted there of the offence in respect of which the order was made, and the order may thereafter be dealt with and enforced by the court to which it is so transferred in all respects as if that court had made the order.
@ref s 742.5(1) (src:15965)
GIVEN `the offender is bound by a conditional sentence order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 territorial division: the offender becomes a resident of a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a supervisor has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is a court of the other territorial division that would, having regard to the mode of trial of the offender, have had jurisdiction to make the order there if the offender had been tried and convicted there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the two territorial divisions are in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings that led to the order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.5(1) the court that made the order may transfer the order to a court in that other territorial division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offender is bound by a conditional sentence order`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offender who is bound by a conditional sentence order becomes a resident" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `s 2 territorial division: the offender becomes a resident of a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "becomes a resident of a territorial division, other than the territorial division where the order was made" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `s 2 territorial division: the offender becomes a resident of a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): section 2's "territorial division" is not covered on these facts
        IF NOT (`a supervisor has applied`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the application of a supervisor" (an "on" gate on a "may", treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `the consents of subsection (1.1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to subsection (1.1)", which says the transfer "may be granted only with" a consent that is missing
        IF NOT (`the court is a court of the other territorial division that would, having regard to the mode of trial of the offender, have had jurisdiction to make the order there if the offender had been tried and convicted there`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "transfer the order to a court in that other territorial division that would ... have had jurisdiction" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- when subsection (1.1) names no consent for the case (neither paragraph's "if" holds) it restricts nothing: fork F-12, the other reading is NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the consents of subsection (1.1)` MEANS
            `s 742.5(1.1) the transfer may be granted with the consents given` `the two territorial divisions are in the same province` `the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made consented` `the proceedings that led to the order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` `the Attorney General of Canada consented`

DECLARE `s 742.5(2) other court` IS ONE OF
