§§ `742.6(3) to (5) The hearing; consent; adjournment; report`

-- src:15988 | (3) The hearing of an allegation of a breach of condition shall be commenced within thirty days, or as soon thereafter as is practicable, after
-- src:15989 | (a) the offender’s arrest; or
-- src:15990 | (b) the compelling of the offender’s appearance in accordance with paragraph (1)(d).
@ref s 742.6(3) (src:15988-15990)
GIVEN `the days from the arrest, or from the compelling of the appearance, to the commencement of the hearing` IS A NUMBER
      `the hearing was commenced as soon after the thirty days as was practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(3) the hearing of the allegation was commenced in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the days from the arrest, or from the compelling of the appearance, to the commencement of the hearing` AT MOST 30 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the hearing was commenced as soon after the thirty days as was practicable` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be commenced within thirty days, or as soon thereafter as is practicable" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a))

DECLARE `s 742.6(3.1) place` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.6(3.1) the place where the breach is alleged to have been committed`
    `s 742.6(3.1) the place where the offender is found, arrested or in custody`
    `s 742.6(3.1) another place`

-- src:15992 | (3.1) The allegation may be heard by any court having jurisdiction to hear that allegation in the place where the breach is alleged to have been committed or the offender is found, arrested or in custody.
@ref s 742.6(3.1) (src:15992)
GIVEN `the court has jurisdiction to hear that allegation` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `s 742.6(3.1) place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(3.1) the allegation may be heard by the court in the place` MEANS
    IF `the court has jurisdiction to hear that allegation` AND NOT (place EQUALS `s 742.6(3.1) another place`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any court having jurisdiction to hear that allegation in the place where the breach is alleged to have been committed or the offender is found, arrested or in custody"

-- src:15994 | (3.2) If the place where the offender is found, arrested or in custody is outside the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed, no proceedings in respect of that breach shall be instituted in that place without
-- src:15995 | (a) the consent of the Attorney General of the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed; or
-- src:15996 | (b) the consent of the Attorney General of Canada, if the proceedings that led to the issuance of the conditional sentence order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 742.6(3.2) (src:15994-15996)
GIVEN `the place where the offender is found, arrested or in custody is outside the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings that led to the order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(3.2) proceedings in that place are barred for want of consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the place where the offender is found, arrested or in custody is outside the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the place ... is outside the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed" (a bar whose "if" is unmet)
        IF `the Attorney General of the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed consented`
           OR (`the proceedings that led to the order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` AND `the Attorney General of Canada consented`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no proceedings ... shall be instituted in that place without (a) the consent ... ; or (b) the consent ..." (the text reads "or": one consent is enough; fork F-5, the other reading requires every consent the case calls for)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15998 | (3.3) A judge may, at any time during a hearing of an allegation of breach of condition, adjourn the hearing for a reasonable period.
@ref s 742.6(3.3) (src:15998)
GIVEN `the time is during a hearing of an allegation of breach of condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(3.3) the judge may adjourn the hearing for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the time is during a hearing of an allegation of breach of condition`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A judge may, at any time during a hearing of an allegation of breach of condition, adjourn" (a "during" gate on a "may", treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `the period is a reasonable period` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a reasonable period"

-- src:16000 | (4) An allegation of a breach of condition must be supported by a written report of the supervisor, which report must include, where appropriate, signed statements of witnesses.
@ref s 742.6(4) (src:16000)
GIVEN `the report is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is the report of the supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes, where appropriate, signed statements of witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(4) the allegation of breach is supported by the written report the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the report is in writing` AND `the report is the report of the supervisor` AND `the report includes, where appropriate, signed statements of witnesses`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An allegation of a breach of condition must be supported by a written report of the supervisor, which report must include, where appropriate, signed statements of witnesses" (fork F-14)

-- src:16002 | (5) The report is admissible in evidence if the party intending to produce it has, before the hearing, given the offender reasonable notice and a copy of the report.
@ref s 742.6(5) (src:16002)
GIVEN `the party intending to produce the report gave the offender reasonable notice before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party gave the offender a copy of the report before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(5) the report is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the party intending to produce the report gave the offender reasonable notice before the hearing` AND `the party gave the offender a copy of the report before the hearing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report is admissible in evidence if the party intending to produce it has, before the hearing, given the offender reasonable notice and a copy of the report" (an "if" with no "only"; marginal reading, NOTES.md) (fork F-17)

DECLARE `s 742.6(8) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.6(8) the supervisor`
    `s 742.6(8) a witness whose signed statement is included in the report`
    `s 742.6(8) someone else`

-- src:16005 | (8) The offender may, with leave of the court, require the attendance, for cross-examination, of the supervisor or of any witness whose signed statement is included in the report.
@ref s 742.6(8) (src:16005)
GIVEN person IS A `s 742.6(8) person`
      `the court has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(8) the offender may require the attendance of the person for cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the court has given leave` AND NOT (person EQUALS `s 742.6(8) someone else`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The offender may, with leave of the court, require the attendance, for cross-examination, of the supervisor or of any witness whose signed statement is included in the report" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

§§ `742.6(9) to (17) Powers of the court; suspension; time served`

DECLARE `s 742.6(9) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.6(9)(a) take no action`
    `s 742.6(9)(b) change the optional conditions`
    `s 742.6(9)(c) suspend the conditional sentence order and direct that the offender serve in custody a portion of the unexpired sentence, and that the order resume on the offender's release from custody`
    `s 742.6(9)(d) terminate the conditional sentence order and direct that the offender be committed to custody until the expiration of the sentence`
    `s 742.6(9) another action`

-- src:16007 | (9) Where the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender has without reasonable excuse, the proof of which lies on the offender, breached a condition of the conditional sentence order, the court may
-- src:16008 | (a) take no action;
-- src:16009 | (b) change the optional conditions;
-- src:16010 | (c) suspend the conditional sentence order and direct
-- src:16011 | (i) that the offender serve in custody a portion of the unexpired sentence, and
-- src:16012 | (ii) that the conditional sentence order resume on the offender’s release from custody, either with or without changes to the optional conditions; or
-- src:16013 | (d) terminate the conditional sentence order and direct that the offender be committed to custody until the expiration of the sentence.
@ref s 742.6(9) (src:16007-16013)
GIVEN action IS A `s 742.6(9) action`
      `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender has breached a condition of the conditional sentence order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has proved a reasonable excuse for the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(9) the court may take the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender has breached a condition of the conditional sentence order`)) OR `the offender has proved a reasonable excuse for the breach`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender has without reasonable excuse, the proof of which lies on the offender, breached a condition" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF action EQUALS `s 742.6(9) another action` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) to (d) list four actions and do not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The earlier of two optional dates.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE, b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 742.6(10) the earlier of two dates` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN b
    WHEN JUST x THEN `s 742.6(10) the earlier of a date and an optional date` x b

GIVEN x IS A DATE, b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 742.6(10) the earlier of a date and an optional date` MEANS
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
    WHEN JUST y THEN (IF x LESS THAN y THEN JUST x ELSE JUST y)

-- src:16015 | (10) The running of a conditional sentence order imposed on an offender is suspended during the period that ends with the determination of whether a breach of condition had occurred and begins with the earliest of
-- src:16016 | (a) the issuance of a warrant for the arrest of the offender for the alleged breach,
-- src:16017 | (b) the arrest without warrant of the offender for the alleged breach, and
-- src:16018 | (c) the compelling of the offender’s appearance in accordance with paragraph (1)(d).
@ref s 742.6(10) (src:16015-16018)
GIVEN `the day a warrant was issued for the arrest of the offender for the alleged breach` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the offender was arrested without warrant for the alleged breach` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the offender's appearance was compelled in accordance with paragraph (1)(d)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 742.6(10) the day the suspension of the running of the conditional sentence order begins` MEANS
    `s 742.6(10) the earlier of two dates` (`s 742.6(10) the earlier of two dates` `the day a warrant was issued for the arrest of the offender for the alleged breach` `the day the offender was arrested without warrant for the alleged breach`) `the day the offender's appearance was compelled in accordance with paragraph (1)(d)`

GIVEN day IS A DATE, determined IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(10) the day is no later than the determination, if there is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER determined
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST e THEN NOT (day GREATER THAN e)

-- src:16015 | (10) The running of a conditional sentence order imposed on an offender is suspended during the period that ends with the determination of whether a breach of condition had occurred and begins with the earliest of
@ref s 742.6(10) (src:16015)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      begin IS A MAYBE DATE
      determined IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(10) the running of the conditional sentence order is suspended on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER begin
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no warrant, arrest without warrant or compelled appearance has occurred, so the period has not begun
    WHEN JUST b THEN
        IF day LESS THAN b
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "suspended during the period that ends with the determination ... and begins with the earliest of" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); the day of the determination is taken as inside it, fork F-6)
        ELSE JUST (`s 742.6(10) the day is no later than the determination, if there is one` day determined)

-- src:16020 | (11) If the offender is not detained in custody during any period referred to in subsection (10), the conditions of the order continue to apply, with any changes made to them under section 742.4, and any subsequent breach of those conditions may be dealt with in accordance with this section.
@ref s 742.6(11) (src:16020)
GIVEN `the offender is not detained in custody during the period referred to in subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(11) the conditions of the order continue to apply, with any changes made to them under section 742.4` MEANS
    IF `the offender is not detained in custody during the period referred to in subsection (10)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the offender is not detained in custody during any period referred to in subsection (10)"

-- src:16020 | (11) If the offender is not detained in custody during any period referred to in subsection (10), the conditions of the order continue to apply, with any changes made to them under section 742.4, and any subsequent breach of those conditions may be dealt with in accordance with this section.
@ref s 742.6(11) (src:16020)
GIVEN `the offender is not detained in custody during the period referred to in subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(11) a subsequent breach of those conditions may be dealt with in accordance with section 742.6` MEANS
    IF `the offender is not detained in custody during the period referred to in subsection (10)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the offender is not detained in custody during any period referred to in subsection (10)"

-- src:16022 | (12) A conditional sentence order referred to in subsection (10) starts running again on the making of an order to detain the offender in custody under subsection 515(6) and, unless section 742.7 applies, continues running while the offender is detained under the order.
@ref s 742.6(12) (src:16022)
GIVEN `an order to detain the offender in custody under subsection 515(6) has been made on or before the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is detained under the order on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 742.7 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(12) the conditional sentence order runs on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an order to detain the offender in custody under subsection 515(6) has been made on or before the day`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "starts running again on the making of an order to detain the offender in custody under subsection 515(6)"
        IF NOT (`the offender is detained under the order on the day`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of the period while the offender is detained under the order
        IF `section 742.7 applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless section 742.7 applies, continues running while the offender is detained under the order" (fork F-13)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16024 | (13) Section 6 of the Prisons and Reformatories Act does not apply to the period of detention in custody under subsection 515(6).
@ref s 742.6(13) (src:16024)
GIVEN `the period is a period of detention in custody under subsection 515(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(13) section 6 of the Prisons and Reformatories Act applies to the period` MEANS
    IF `the period is a period of detention in custody under subsection 515(6)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 6 of the Prisons and Reformatories Act does not apply to the period of detention in custody under subsection 515(6)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the period of detention in custody under subsection 515(6)"

-- src:16026 | (14) Despite subsection (10), if there was unreasonable delay in the execution of a warrant, the court may, at any time, order that any period between the issuance and execution of the warrant that it considers appropriate in the interests of justice is deemed to be time served under the conditional sentence order unless the period has been so deemed under subsection (15).
@ref s 742.6(14) (src:16026)
GIVEN `there was unreasonable delay in the execution of a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers the period appropriate in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period has been deemed to be time served under subsection (15)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(14) the court may order that the period between the issuance and execution of the warrant is deemed to be time served` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the period has been deemed to be time served under subsection (15)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the period has been so deemed under subsection (15)" (fork F-13)
        IF `there was unreasonable delay in the execution of a warrant` AND `the court considers the period appropriate in the interests of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if there was unreasonable delay in the execution of a warrant, the court may ... any period ... that it considers appropriate in the interests of justice" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16028 | (15) If the allegation is withdrawn or dismissed or the offender is found to have had a reasonable excuse for the breach, the sum of the following periods is deemed to be time served under the conditional sentence order:
-- src:16029 | (a) any period for which the running of the conditional sentence order was suspended; and
-- src:16030 | (b) if subsection (12) applies, a period equal to one half of the period that the conditional sentence order runs while the offender is detained under an order referred to in that subsection.
@ref s 742.6(15) (src:16028-16030)
GIVEN `the allegation is withdrawn or dismissed or the offender is found to have had a reasonable excuse for the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days for which the running of the conditional sentence order was suspended` IS A NUMBER
      `subsection (12) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days the order ran while the offender was detained under an order referred to in subsection (12)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 742.6(15) the days deemed to be time served under the conditional sentence order` MEANS
    IF `the allegation is withdrawn or dismissed or the offender is found to have had a reasonable excuse for the breach`
    THEN JUST (`the days for which the running of the conditional sentence order was suspended` PLUS (IF `subsection (12) applies` THEN `the days the order ran while the offender was detained under an order referred to in subsection (12)` DIVIDED BY 2 ELSE 0))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the allegation is withdrawn or dismissed or the offender is found to have had a reasonable excuse for the breach" (a number has no FALSE; fork F-4)

-- src:16032 | (16) If a court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender has without reasonable excuse, the proof of which lies on the offender, breached a condition of the conditional sentence order, the court may, in exceptional cases and in the interests of justice, order that some or all of the period of suspension referred to in subsection (10) is deemed to be time served under the conditional sentence order.
@ref s 742.6(16) (src:16032)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender has breached a condition of the conditional sentence order without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(16) the court may order that some or all of the period of suspension is deemed to be time served` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender has breached a condition of the conditional sentence order without reasonable excuse` AND `the case is exceptional` AND `the order is in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a court is satisfied ... the court may, in exceptional cases and in the interests of justice" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

DECLARE `s 742.6(17) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.6(17)(a) the circumstances and seriousness of the breach`
    `s 742.6(17)(b) whether not making the order would cause the offender undue hardship based on the offender's individual circumstances`
    `s 742.6(17)(c) the period for which the offender was subject to conditions while the running of the order was suspended and whether the offender complied with those conditions during that period`
    `s 742.6(17) another matter`

-- src:16034 | (17) In exercising its discretion under subsection (16), a court shall consider
-- src:16035 | (a) the circumstances and seriousness of the breach;
-- src:16036 | (b) whether not making the order would cause the offender undue hardship based on the offender’s individual circumstances; and
-- src:16037 | (c) the period for which the offender was subject to conditions while the running of the conditional sentence order was suspended and whether the offender complied with those conditions during that period.
@ref s 742.6(17) (src:16034-16037)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 742.6(17) matter`
      `the court is exercising its discretion under subsection (16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.6(17) the court shall consider the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the court is exercising its discretion under subsection (16)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In exercising its discretion under subsection (16), a court shall consider" (a duty whose "in" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF matter EQUALS `s 742.6(17) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall consider (a) ... (b) ... (c)" does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 742.7 -- Imprisonment for another offence; multiple sentences`

-- src:16039 | 742.7 (1) If an offender who is subject to a conditional sentence order is imprisoned as a result of a sentence imposed for another offence, whenever committed, the running of the conditional sentence order is suspended during the period of imprisonment for that other offence.
@ref s 742.7(1) (src:16039)
GIVEN `the offender is subject to a conditional sentence order and is imprisoned as a result of a sentence imposed for another offence, whenever committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day falls within the period of imprisonment for that other offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.7(1) the running of the conditional sentence order is suspended on the day` MEANS
    IF `the offender is subject to a conditional sentence order and is imprisoned as a result of a sentence imposed for another offence, whenever committed` AND `the day falls within the period of imprisonment for that other offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offender ... is imprisoned as a result of a sentence imposed for another offence ... the running ... is suspended during the period of imprisonment for that other offence" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a))

-- src:16041 | (2) If an order is made under paragraph 742.6(9)(c) or (d) to commit an offender to custody, the custodial period ordered shall, unless the court considers that it would not be in the interests of justice, be served consecutively to any other period of imprisonment that the offender is serving when that order is made.
@ref s 742.7(2) (src:16041)
GIVEN `an order is made under paragraph 742.6(9)(c) or (d) to commit the offender to custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers that it would not be in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.7(2) the custodial period ordered shall be served consecutively to any other period of imprisonment that the offender is serving` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an order is made under paragraph 742.6(9)(c) or (d) to commit the offender to custody`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is made under paragraph 742.6(9)(c) or (d) to commit an offender to custody" (a duty whose "if" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF `the court considers that it would not be in the interests of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court considers that it would not be in the interests of justice" (fork F-13)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 742.7(3) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.7(3) the purpose of section 743.1`
    `s 742.7(3) the purpose of section 139 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`
    `s 742.7(3) another purpose`

-- src:16043 | (3) If an offender is serving both a custodial period referred to in subsection (2) and any other period of imprisonment, the periods shall, for the purpose of section 743.1 and section 139 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, be deemed to constitute one sentence of imprisonment.
@ref s 742.7(3) (src:16043)
GIVEN `the offender is serving both a custodial period referred to in subsection (2) and any other period of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 742.7(3) purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.7(3) the periods are deemed to constitute one sentence of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the offender is serving both a custodial period referred to in subsection (2) and any other period of imprisonment` AND NOT (purpose EQUALS `s 742.7(3) another purpose`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of section 743.1 and section 139 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act"

DECLARE `s 742.7(4) release` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.7(4) release on parole`
    `s 742.7(4) release on statutory release`
    `s 742.7(4) release on earned remission`
    `s 742.7(4) the expiration of the sentence`
    `s 742.7(4) another release`

-- src:16045 | (4) The running of any period of the conditional sentence order that is to be served in the community resumes upon the release of the offender from prison on parole, on statutory release, on earned remission, or at the expiration of the sentence.
@ref s 742.7(4) (src:16045)
GIVEN release IS A `s 742.7(4) release`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.7(4) the running of the period of the conditional sentence order that is to be served in the community resumes` MEANS
    CONSIDER release
    WHEN `s 742.7(4) release on parole` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.7(4) release on statutory release` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.7(4) release on earned remission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.7(4) the expiration of the sentence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.7(4) another release` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "on parole, on statutory release, on earned remission, or at the expiration of the sentence" does not say "only"
